  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1211 AM CST Thu Nov 26 2026\n\nThe long term will be characterized by warmer temperatures and dry \nweather. The overall longwave pattern has a dampened upper trough \nover the central CONUS allowing for a couple days of warming and \nmostly dry conditions ahead of the next cold front. That cold front \nwill arrive on Sunday as a dry front for Central TX and very polar \njet dominated in character. The pattern dampens quickly by Monday \nand with southerlies to return rather quickly Tuesday we wouldn't \nanticipate any new freezes in the wake of this front. Another \nwarming and dry SW surface wind pattern should bring back a period \nof above normal temperatures by mid week. A polar disturbance could \nbe in the works for next Thursday, and that might give our next hope \nfor some rain.",
